  "full_text": "So there's two ways to control your weight, moderation and grace. The Native American approach is grace, which is, you know, you can't find any food, we're starving. So God feeds the sparrows, so there's a promise that don't worry about what you'll eat or drink, because God will provide it. But as a matter of fact, he didn't say you won't hunger and as a matter of fact the hunger state of mind is a spiritual experience and Now the prodigal son story Demonstrates that The prodigal ends up higher in the kingdom than the good son and that doesn't seem like that seems unfair But he had to go through the humiliation and the corresponding exaltation and the learning experience. And no pain, no gain. And he went through the pain of humiliation. And anyway, maybe he got more pain than the good son. I don't know. So it doesn't sound fair, but I think it's true. Now, Prometheus was a father of forethought. supposedly he got his guts ripped out every day by the gods. And well, so the Native Americans don't do well in a forethought society. So not everybody is, well, some people are just not modern men, I guess. Whether they're saved or not is another question. But we're talking about killing the fat people. so i don't know um you know there's um throughout god through everything's possible with god i don't know but anyway",
